{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "scale-county-runspec",
    "description": "PENDING (PLAN.md §7.3.45, step 7f). `scale-county`: Total Energy (91) for the gasoline passenger car at Washtenaw County SINGLE scale, August 2020, weekday, hour 7, from the default database plus Washtenaw's COMPLETE county database (`inputs/washtenaw-county.esm`, built from moves.rs `setup-county.sql`). MOVESOutput is 729 rows: running exhaust (9101) on road types 1 to 5, 125 rows each, and start exhaust (9102) on road type 1, 104 rows. The RunSpec also names petroleum and fossil energy (92, 93) and well-to-pump (99), which are not MOVES5 pollutant-processes, and extended idle (9190), which a passenger car never emits. It does NOT reproduce yet. `n_outputRate` is bound to what THIS chain computes (104, start exhaust's block) so the document runs and says where it stops; `run_selectionUnported` is 4.\n\nTHE COUNTY DATABASE IS NOT WHAT IT WAITS ON, MEASURED 2026-10-20. Every one of the 729 MOVESOutput rows equals the DEFAULT-domain `expand-roadtypes` snapshot's row at the same key, at the six-digit rendering (same county, year, month, hour and vehicle; that RunSpec selects road types 1 to 5 explicitly). The two execution databases differ only in MOVES's SINGLE-scale REPLACE tables, which hold the 2020 rows the run reads, in `avft`, which leaves `sampleVehiclePopulation` the default's, and in the 9190 selection. And the domain document is checked on its own: `process-crankcase-start`'s selections mounted on `inputs/washtenaw-county.esm` emit a relation byte-identical to the DEFAULT run's, and reproduce `process-crankcase-start-single`'s oracle at its worst cell, 8.250e-06 (1.3e-10 to 2.1e-10 from the starts county database, its twelve-decimal truncation).\n\nWHAT IT WAITS ON is the road type as an AXIS, which `expand-roadtypes` waits on identically:\n\n* Running exhaust on FOUR on-network road types. Selecting road type 1 beside a running process makes MOVES select every road type (\"Off-Network Idle requires all roadtypes\"), so `runspecroadtype` holds 1 to 5. The model has one on-network road type, `run_roadTypeID`, a scalar: summed over four rows it reads 14, the zone and county joins find nothing, and every row comes out at county 0. `run_selectionUnported` counts it (3 for the extra on-network road types, 1 for an on-road process beside road type 1). The activity (SHO by road type: VMT x roadTypeVMTFraction over the road's speed) and the rate (the average-speed operating-mode distribution, `pp_W`, per road type) both need the axis; the forward closure of `run_roadTypeID` is 283 of `onroad/model.esm`'s 1,036 equations.\n* OFF-NETWORK IDLE, running exhaust on road type 1 (TotalActivityGenerator step 190c): per age, ONI SHO = max(S x (totalIdleFraction - SD/S) / (1 - totalIdleFraction), 0), with S the on-network SHO summed over road types 2-5 and SD the same weighted by each road's `drivingIdleFraction`. Reproduced in pandas from the execution database's `sho`, `drivingidlefraction` and `totalidlefraction` (idle region 103, county type 1): 41 of 41 ages at 3.9e-06. `drivingIdleFraction` is operating mode 1's share of the road's speed-weighted operating-mode distribution (moves.rs baserategenerator/drivecycle.rs:427-492), so it is a contraction of the per-road `pp_W` the first item builds; `totalIdleFraction` is a default table this model does not yet mount.\n* A pollutant-process emitted on SEVERAL road types. The output relation's blocks are pollutant-processes, each on ONE road type (`rspp_rateRoadTypeID`); running energy here is one pollutant-process on five, so a block becomes a (pollutant-process, road type) pair.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "pending",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle"
    ]
  },
